  "behavior": [
    "Substrate and Solana grants have independent in-memory revisions per origin, covering authorization identity, explicit allowed status and protocol-specific accounts. Revoke/restore invalidates an older queued request; unrelated protocol changes do not.",
    "Admission waits for loading, reads the current private cache synchronously and captures its revision in private queue state. Final checks reject missing legacy revisions and compare current grant scope/revision before key access and signature release.",
    "Substrate checks after phishing and after asynchronous local/mobile signing. Solana checks after phishing and send-capability waits, fetches current accounts after those waits, and rechecks key export, broadcaster invocation and result release.",
    "Substrate and EVM external-signature completion now use the same per-request pending ownership and current authorization/context guards. Solana continues to reject external-signature completion. Cryptographic verification of externally supplied bytes is not added by this checkpoint.",
    "Account-list queries read current grants after their load barrier and require explicit true flags, so revocation or malformed truthy flags cannot expose the authorized Substrate/Solana account lists.",
    "A stale Solana result after broadcaster invocation is consumed without releasing signed bytes or starting another broadcaster call. An already dispatched transaction cannot be recalled; the RPC client may continue its existing identical-byte endpoint failover."
  ],
